messages.content:
Review brief:
Prepare a focused review of how water-matrix effects should be tested and reported so that PFAS treatment performance can be translated beyond clean laboratory water.

Required components:
[{"requirement":"Compare how organic matter, surfactants, inorganic ions, and other co-solutes alter physical separation and degradation processes."},{"requirement":"Distinguish inhibitory, promotive, neutral, and interactive effects and relate them to treatment mechanism and PFAS properties."},{"requirement":"Recommend a minimum matrix-characterization and matched-control framework for defensible cross-study comparison."}]

Task boundaries:
{"constraints":[{"material_violation_rule":"Triggers if one matrix constituent is assigned a universal effect across PFAS structures, constituent concentrations, and treatment mechanisms."},{"material_violation_rule":"Triggers if clean-water performance is generalized to real water without matrix characterization and matched controls, or if separation is conflated with destruction."}],"task_boundaries":"Water-matrix effects on PFAS physical separation and degradation and the design of matched, matrix-representative experiments."}

Held-out anchor identifiers:
{"all_blocked_dois":["10.1016/j.hazadv.2023.100322"],"all_blocked_titles":["effects of water matrix on per and poly fluoroalkyl substances pfas treatment physical separation and degradation processes a review"],"all_blocked_urls":["https://doi.org/10.1016/j.hazadv.2023.100322"],"anchor_id":"AR-ZEIDABADI-2023","corpus_source":"2023 - Zeidabadi - Effects of water matrix on per- and poly-fluoroalkyl substances (PFAS) treatment - Physical-separation and degradation processes - A review.pdf","doi":"10.1016/j.hazadv.2023.100322","title":"Effects of water matrix on per- and poly-fluoroalkyl substances (PFAS) treatment: Physical-separation and degradation processes - A review","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.hazadv.2023.100322"}

